{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Eat it today, for today is a sabbath to HaShem; today you will not find it in the field.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory interpreted: 'today you will not find it' — but for the world to come you will find it. The explanation of this is that on the day of Sabbath they did not find the manna, but for the world to come they will find the foundation of the manna, which is the supernal light itself. And the word היום ('today') is mentioned three times in the verse, alluding to the three meals of Sabbath." "<b>And here I am</b> revealing a secret that the masters of truth concealed concerning the three meals, and I shall allude to it for you here. And I say that the first meal is the meal of the night; it is the attribute of שמור ('guard') and is called by the name Malkhut, and from this our Sages of blessed memory enlightened our eyes, for they would say on Sabbath eve: 'Come, let us go forth to greet the bride — the Sabbath Queen,' and they would say: 'Come, O bride; come, O bride.' And therefore he mentioned first אכלוהו היום ('eat it today'), for the word אכלוהו is from the language of כלה ('bride'), and one does not betroth the man but only the woman. The second meal is that of the morning, and it alludes to the attribute of Yated (Foundation) called the great Sabbath, and the essence of holiness is only by day, and therefore it is called קדוש היום קדושא רבא ('the holiness of the day, the great holiness'); and likewise in the prayer of evening and morning we say אהבת עולם ('an everlasting love'), and that of the morning our Sages of blessed memory call אהבה רבה ('a great love'). And it is known that the night is שמור ('guarded') and the day is זכור ('remembered'), and therefore he said: כי שבת היום לה' ('for today is a sabbath to HaShem'). The third meal is that of the afternoon, and it is the seal of the day, alluding to ראשית הראשית ('the beginning of the beginning'), which is the principal of the structure and its head, and therefore he said: היום לא תמצאוהו ('today you will not find it'), for the word לא is like אין, as in והחכמה מאין תמצא ('and wisdom shall be found from nothing'). All this is from below upward, and they are meals for the soul in the true life, in enduring and eternal delight. From now on, understand the greatness of the merit of one who fulfills the three meals, and his reward and his great merit through this great and supernal intention."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "The printed text reads שחרית in parentheses after ערבית in the phrase תפלת (שחרית) ערבית; read as 'the prayer of evening and morning' per context. The word יסוד is rendered literally as Yated (Foundation) in reference to the sefirah; the author appears to use the form יסוד rather than יסוד."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:18.668773130Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}